body = ("**FIX-T2 PAUSED WITH ITS CURE BUILT AND PROVED AGAINST A REAL PARSER:** the population measured with offsets classified against `@babel/parser` — `BARE_LOADING` raw 32, THREE in comments (`GalleryTopbar.jsx:81`, `RealmUnfurlLoading.jsx:22`, `WorldMapStage.jsx:285`), code-only 29; `NULL_FALLBACK` raw 38, ONE in a comment (`TurnstileGate.jsx:12` — the exact match that cost FIX-P3 a cycle), code-only 37; all four are sentences ABOUT the debt counted AS the debt. THE CURE: a second export `commentsOnly` in `tests/helpers/codeOnlySource.js` (comments blanked; strings, templates, regex and JSX text kept; OFFSETS PRESERVED; purely additive — zero deleted lines, `codeOnly`'s 22 importers untouched); over 5,148 files it agrees with `@babel/parser` byte-for-byte (0 comment chars kept, 0 code chars blanked); three ablations prove each piece load-bearing (dropping regex tracking blanks 5,771 chars of real code across 230 files; skipping `${…}` leaves 572 comment chars standing — which REFUTED a cannot-catch the lane had already written into the header, so it rewrote the scanner rather than ship a false claim); the `/>` ambiguity settled by scoring six candidate rules. PINS SHRINK-ONLY: 32 → 29, 38 → 37, rawButton's budget 39 → 36; the file's old header rule ('COMMENT lines included by design') overturned in place; the fixture inline — no new file. THE SWEEP: the brief's grep found 1 file; a structural scan of all 178 `tests/lint` files found 54 candidates → 7 in the class proper: 5 CURED (loadingNarration, rawButton, errorCopy, forkedColor, significanceMigration), 2 LEFT (clamp/slugify baselines — they strip already, with a string-blind regex pair); left BY DESIGN: `negativeAssertionAnchor.walker` (counts `// anchored:` markers on purpose), `sizeBaseline` (immune via eslint's `skipComments`). 51 local stripper copies estate-wide, 27 string-blind → TOOL-20's roster. THE CHAIR'S TWO RULINGS (vetoable): (1) `significanceMigration.census.test.js` appears RED at 6a3e8089f by the lane's replication (class-A pins 40/20; raw 41/21; stripped 40/20 — the extra file `bandFamilies.js:34-35`, a JSDoc quoting `significance === 'major'`, landed 2026-08-04) yet run 21 at c33446830 named ONE red and not this file → the lane runs it UNEDITED first and settles it by execution; if red, the reconciliation is owed (the ratchet's exclusions, an env gate, or a counting difference) before any conclusion; if green, the cure moves no pin; (2) CURE-J's `stripComments` (DIGEST-grade: keeps `${…}` comments, collapses whitespace, destroys offsets — the safe direction for an identity) and FIX-T2's `commentsOnly` (COUNTER-grade: blanks, preserves offsets) are TWO INSTRUMENTS with distinct contracts, not a duplicate — ACCEPTED; each header names the other; TOOL-20 routes counters to `commentsOnly` and identities to `stripComments`; the counts are identical under both (29/29, 37/37 — the whitespace-collapse prediction confirmed). Also: `rawButtonBaseline`'s own header asked for this cure twice and was refused as chair-gated; its fear is now measured true; `PricingTierCards.jsx` leaves the baseline (its only `<button` is a comment) and is linted by name at the gate — if it errors the row returns at budget 37. "
 "**STAGED THIS SITTING (the kit):** the §934.71 shift record DRAFT (`drafts/2026-09-20-cure-j-provenance.DRAFT.json` — `ownerWords` PENDING; the door sequence spelled; it becomes a record only with the owner's verbatim words pasted in and is committed at `docs/shift-records/` on the branch at the flip sitting); the briefs `TOOL-22.md` (the sanctioned `--reseal`: archive under `<ID>.sealed-at-<head>`, never overwrite, `resealedFrom` in the new capsule; six fixture arms) and `TOOL-24.md` (four shrink-only prose-byte totals by the M3 rule — generators · domain-product · certification · `src/data` minus the ten declared leaves — with the declared-row door and a `process.stdout.write` diagnostic on the red; a new `tests/lint` file with its mutation row). SEATS: working = FIX-D9 (walker) · FIX-T2 (paused) · TOOL-19 · TOOL-15; gate = EM-B1f (batch 4) · FIX-C2b · FIX-P1b; queue = FIX-B2 (exclusive, alone) → FIX-D9 → FIX-T2 → FIX-K1 → TOOL-7a → TOOL-9 → TOOL-8a → FIX-P2 → FIX-D7 → FIX-T1 → FIX-D8 → the dead agents.")
line = ("- **§934.47 addendum 90 — FIX-T2 PAUSED: THE COMMENT-RESIDENT POPULATION IS FOUR (3 + 1), THE PINS SHRINK 32 → 29 / 38 → 37, FIVE RATCHETS CURED BY A PARSER-PROVED COUNTER-GRADE STRIPPER (`commentsOnly`, offsets preserved) — RULED A SECOND INSTRUMENT BESIDE CURE-J's DIGEST-GRADE ONE, NOT A DUPLICATE; `significanceMigration` SETTLED BY EXECUTION FIRST; TOOL-20's ROSTER 51/27; THE §934.71 SHIFT-RECORD DRAFT AND THE TOOL-22/TOOL-24 BRIEFS STAGED (2026-09-20 " + stamp + " EDT; the chair; vetoable).** " + body)
u = io.open(ODQ, encoding="utf-8").read()
key = "- **§934.47 addendum 89 —"; assert u.count(key) == 1 and "addendum 90 —" not in u
